Food and water are the two survival meters in ''Human Host''. Both deplete over time and must be replenished from consumable items.

'''Early Access status:''' the meters are active and gameplay-affecting, but restoration is currently limited to looted and foraged consumables. There are no natural water bodies, no water collection, no cooking, no huntable wildlife, and no player-crafted food or drink in the current build.

== The two meters ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Stat !! Depletes at !! Empty consequence
|-
| '''Food''' || Roughly 1% / minute at rest || Health drain begins, stamina cap reduced
|-
| '''Water''' || Roughly 2% / minute at rest || Faster health drain, movement slowdown
|-
|}

Sprinting, combat, mining, and hot biomes ([[Desert]], [[Warzone]]) accelerate depletion. Cold biomes ([[Winter Forest]], [[Winter Town]]) accelerate food specifically.

Internal fields on <code>Char_Status</code>: <code>_currentFood</code> / <code>_maxFood</code>, <code>_currentWater</code> / <code>_maxWater</code>.

