Bottled Water is the reliable staple. Fruit Juice, Soda, and Energy Drink also restore water, and some may carry secondary effects (fill amount / stamina / speed buffs); those should be verified in-game and added to individual item pages.

== Related perks ==

Two Survive-tree factors on <code>Char_Skills</code> directly affect the meters:

* <code>_foodWaterDecrease_Factor</code>: reduces depletion rate (see [[Efficient Metabolism]])
* <code>_adrlinWaterCost_Factor</code>: reduces water consumption at low health (adrenaline)

See [[Perks]] for the full factor catalog.

== Practical tips ==

* '''Loot every zombie.''' Water bottles and canned goods are the primary drops.
* '''Forage as you move.''' Mushrooms, cactuses, and pine cones are cheap fills that cost only a few seconds.
* '''Prioritize containers.''' Loot containers concentrate canned food and bottled drinks.
* '''Slow depletion beats fill rate.''' The Efficient Metabolism factor is worth investing in early.

